        "calls": 5,
        "title": "Release HTTP client adds redirect limit and retry support",
        "summary": "The shared release HTTP client now caps redirect chains at 10, follows 303/307/308 in addition to 301/302, rejects redirect responses missing a Location header, and exposes a withRetries helper that retries transient failures with exponential backoff and a maxAttempts cap. The CLI release wrappers for codebuff and freebuff call downloadAndExtract through withRetries(CONFIG.downloadMaxAttempts), pass CONFIG.downloadRequestTimeout to httpGet, and log retry attempts, so flaky downloads and long redirect loops no longer fail upgrades silently. This hardens the binary download path so a transient network error or a misbehaving registry/CDN redirect no longer blocks installs or updates on any tier.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "In cli/release/http.js (and identically in cli/release-staging/http.js and freebuff/cli/release/http.js), the httpGet function gains redirectCount tracking, a maxRedirects cap of 10, handling for 303/307/308 status codes, and a new withRetries function exported from createReleaseHttpClient. In cli/release/index.js (and identically in the staging and freebuff counterparts), downloadBinary is refactored to call a new downloadAndExtract helper wrapped in withRetries using CONFIG.downloadMaxAttempts, CONFIG.downloadRequestTimeout, isRetryableDownloadStatus, isRetryableDownloadError, retry messaging, and a new pipeline import from stream/promises.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "high",
        "unknowns": "The exact rollout of these retry/redirect changes and whether freebuff's downstream binary download endpoint already enforces the new redirect limit are not visible in the diff.",
