      "facts": [
        "Abort any in-flight run BEFORE resetting the store and switching chats: an orphaned run would keep checkpointing, and its writes could land in the resumed chat's directory, overwriting that transcript.",
        "Abort any in-flight run BEFORE clearing state and rotating the chat id: an orphaned run would keep streaming after the switch and its late checkpoints/final save would persist the old conversation's state under the new chat (or vice versa).",
        "Let chat switches abort this run so it can't keep streaming (and persisting) for a conversation the user has left.",
        "Already aborted (e.g. Esc, or a second chat switch): don't schedule again, the store may hold the next conversation's messages by now.",
        "Drop any queued/in-flight async checkpoint first so a stale write can't land after this authoritative final save."
      ],
      "title": "CLI update: app",
      "summary": "New files: `cli/src/utils/active-run.ts`.",
