      "significance": "notable",
      "hasDiff": true,
      "ai": {
        "model": "deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 11,
        "title": "CLI aborts in-flight run before chat switches to prevent cross-chat",
        "summary": "A new registry in `cli/src/utils/active-run.ts` tracks the in-flight agent run's abort hook, and `abortActiveRun()` is now called from `cli/src/app.tsx` `handleResumeChat` and `handleNewChat` and the `/new` command handler before resetting the chat store or rotating the chat id. In `cli/src/hooks/use-send-message.ts`, each run captures its own chat directory into `runChatDir` and registers an aborter that skips re-scheduling when already aborted, while `runChatIsCurrent()` gates every `saveChatState` and `scheduleCheckpointSave` call so a chat switch stops the run from persisting its (now-stale) messages into a different conversation's transcript.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "New file `cli/src/utils/active-run.ts` exports `setActiveRunAborter`, `clearActiveRunAborter`, `abortActiveRun`, and `resolveCurrentChatDir`; `abortActiveRun()` is invoked from `handleResumeChat` and `handleNewChat` in `cli/src/app.tsx` and from the `/new` command handler in `cli/src/commands/command-registry.ts` before store reset and `startNewChat`. In `cli/src/hooks/use-send-message.ts`, `setActiveRunAborter(aiMessageId, ...)` registers a per-run aborter guarded against double-abort; `runChatDir` is captured at run start and `runChatIsCurrent()` gates persistence so a mid-run chat switch stops the active run from streaming and checkpointing into another chat's directory.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "high",
        "unknowns": "The diff does not describe a specific user-observable symptom or rollout plan beyond the in-code comments.",
